__pycache__
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info
.venv
venv
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache

# Go module vendor directories (services/*/vendor). The bare pattern also matches the web app's
# /vendor route, so the negation below keeps the Vendor Portal frontend tracked (ADR-030).
vendor
!/apps/web/src/app/vendor/

# Prisma
backend/prisma/migrations/**/migration_lock.toml

# Docker
.docker

# Test artifacts
test-results
playwright-report
# Pact consumer contracts — generated by contract tests (tests/contract); regenerated each run
pacts

# cos-audit (content is git-ignored, directory committed)
cos-audit/*
!cos-audit/.gitkeep

# Stryker mutation testing artifacts (QM-1)
# Leading-slash-free patterns that contain a slash are anchored to this file's directory, so a bare
# `reports/mutation/` only ignored the repo root. Mutation runs are per-package
# (`pnpm --filter @cos/financial test:mutation` → packages/@cos/financial/reports/mutation/), so the
# pattern must match at any depth or every run leaves an untracked ~250 KB HTML report behind.
**/.stryker-tmp/
**/reports/mutation/

# Terraform working state. `terraform init` downloads provider binaries into .terraform/ (hundreds
# of MB) and plan/apply write tfstate — none of it belongs in git, and none of it was ignored, so a
# single `terraform init` left committable artifacts behind.
# .terraform.lock.hcl is deliberately NOT ignored: HashiCorp's guidance is to commit the provider
# lock file so every environment resolves identical provider versions.
**/.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
crash.log
override.tf
override_*.tf

# Rule 38 local gate state. `.claude/` is otherwise COMMITTED in this repository — rules, hooks,
# skills, agents and commands all live there and are tracked — so these two are named explicitly
# rather than covered by a directory rule.
#   impl-approved  is the product owner's approval marker, and it is exactly what
#                  .claude/hooks/rule-38-check-approval.sh reads before allowing a .ts/.tsx/.sql
#                  write. Committing one would arrive pre-approved in every clone and every CI
#                  checkout, disarming the only human gate in the workflow for everybody, silently.
#   impl-pending.md is one session's working plan, superseded by the next.
#   impl-completed-*.md is the SAME artefact after the fact. One was committed on 2026-09-06 — a
#                  verbatim copy of a pending plan, made to preserve the previous round's record
#                  before the file was overwritten — and it turned CI's Lint job red with 20
#                  MD013 line-length errors, because a session plan is written to be read in a
#                  terminal, not to pass a document linter. The record it holds is not lost:
#                  the decisions it lists are also in the ADRs, the screens README and the code
#                  comments that cite them.
.claude/impl-approved
.claude/impl-pending.md
.claude/impl-completed-*.md
#   archive/ is the same artefact under a third name. `.claude/archive/impl-pending-*.md`
#                  appeared on 2026-09-10 when one round's plan was set aside to make room
#                  for the next, and it turned Lint red with 18 MD013 errors — the identical
#                  failure the paragraph above records, four days later and one filename
#                  along. Naming the DIRECTORY rather than a fourth pattern is what stops a
#                  fifth.
.claude/archive/

# ── Generated prompt bundles, kept beside the repo rather than in it ─────────────────────────────
#
# `docs/Claude outputs/` appeared on 2026-09-10 holding a README and a .zip of Stitch prompts, and
# turned the Lint job red twice over: prettier on the README, and markdownlint with six MD013
# line-length errors — one line 404 characters long. That is the same shape of failure the
# impl-*.md entries above record: a working document written to be read, linted as if it were
# reference documentation.
#
# IT IS ALSO NOT A DOCS DIRECTORY THIS REPOSITORY HAS. `.claude/rules/markdown-docs.md` fixes the
# set — api · architecture · assessments · evidence · manual · policies · registers · research ·
# runbooks · screens · specifications — and a name carrying a space and a capital needs quoting in
# every shell command that touches it. A `.zip` is not a form `docs/` stores either.
#
# Product-owner decision 2026-09-10: keep it out of the repository. If any of it should be kept,
# `docs/research/` is where prompt material of this kind belongs, as Markdown that passes the
# linters like every other document.
docs/Claude outputs/
